{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Malitavambha","html":"<article id='thag1.105'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.105 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.105 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekādasamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Eleven </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Malitavambhattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Malitavambha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ukkaṇṭhitopi na vase, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Dissatisfied, one should not stay; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ramamānopi pakkame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and even if happy, one should leave. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tvevānatthasaṁhitaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who sees clearly wouldn’t stay </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vase vāsaṁ vicakkhaṇo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in a place that was not conducive to the goal. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Malitavambho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
